g-logo.svg is Google's "G" logo, as Google's own "Sign in with Google"
button draws it, used unchanged as Google's branding guidelines
(https://developers.google.com/identity/branding-guidelines) allow, to stand
for signing in with Google. Google and the Google logo are trademarks of
Google LLC.

Sign in's "G" is docs/specs/assets/google-g.svg, which logos.rs takes from the
spec as it is. It is Google's "G" from Google's "Sign in with Google" button
for Android and the web, Android + Web/SVG/Light/Theme=Light, Show text=No,
Shape=Square, Platform=Android+Web.svg, from
https://developers.google.com/static/identity/images/signin-assets.zip, with
the button's fill and stroke left out and cropped to the "G", which is drawn
unchanged, as Google's sign-in branding guidelines
(https://developers.google.com/identity/branding-guidelines) ask.
